# Build-context exclusions for the backend production image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING
# The Dockerfile compiles better-sqlite3 in a builder stage, copies the result
# with `COPY --from=builder /app/node_modules ./node_modules`, and then runs
# `COPY . .`. That second copy overwrites the compiled node_modules with
# whatever happens to sit in the build context. Without this file the image is
# only correct when the context is clean -- which is true on the VPS (it builds
# straight after `git reset --hard origin/main`) and false on every developer
# machine. A local build produced an image that died on boot with
# NODE_MODULE_VERSION 127 vs 137 because the host's Node 22 binary shadowed the
# image's Node 24 one.
#
# It is also a data-and-secret boundary. A local build was shipping /app/.env
# and a diagnosticpro.db holding 113 diagnostic_submissions rows into the
# production image. `.env` is gitignored, and `git reset --hard` does NOT delete
# ignored files, so a stray .env on the deploy host would be baked in too.
# Excluding them here makes the image identical no matter where it is built.

# Dependencies -- always supplied by the builder stage, never the context.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets. .env.example is intentionally still shipped as documentation.
.env
*.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local databases and their WAL/journal siblings.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Test, coverage and authoring artifacts -- not needed at runtime.
__tests__
coverage
claudes-docs
.harness-hash

# Generated report output; the container writes reports to the /data volume.
reports

# VCS and build metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
